summary:
  A device's refusal is read out of the first 200 characters of its answer,
  where the reason is not.

history:
  A Ruark R5se answered three station addresses with HTTP 500 and a SOAP
  fault naming UPnP error 716, "Resource not found", and played a fourth
  (2026-11-12). The helper kept the first 200 characters of the answer and
  the errorCode sits 270 in, so all the widget could say was "Could not
  cast", the same words it has for a speaker that is switched off. The
  fault is now read out of the whole answer and the line names the code.

target:
  package/contents/ui/cast.py

find:
          raise SoapFault(control_url, status, headers, action, data)

replace:
          raise SoapFault(control_url, status, headers, action, data[:200])

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cast_fault.py::test_a_refused_address_is_named_by_the_code_the_device_gave.
